<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Incheon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chemulpo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Incheon is a port city on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-sea">Yellow Sea</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a>. Opened to foreign trade as Chemulpo in 1883, it became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>'s main gateway to the capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/occupation-of-japan">American occupation</a> troops landed there in September 1945, and in September 1950 General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douglas-macarthur">Douglas MacArthur</a>'s amphibious landing at Incheon turned the course of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a>. It is now the site of South Korea's main international airport.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/incheon.jpg" alt="Incheon" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jaehyuk Lee · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Songdo_Central_Park_and_Posco_Tower_Songdo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
